          "en": "Use when a manoeuvre is claimed that a body cannot perform — the corner bound applied to mass. horo/cornerLimit gives the kinematics; this adds the body: F = m·v²/r, which has candidates. Every route around the bound must change one factor — inertial mass, proper acceleration, the body, or the observation — and each is a named claim with a refuting test. Computes what each hypothesis COSTS: the factor by which it must exceed its own measured bound. Identifies no object and proposes no mechanism."
