          "en": "Use when reasoning about the cost-to-act atom of a market — the total effort plus price between wanting and having. 'Convenient' means low friction; it is the lever convenience and engineering play. Coupled to status with opposite sign (the effort is often the signal), so lowering it decays exclusivity — sequence the two, do not try to maximise both."
